{"The DRINK CHEER-UP COFFEE wall clock read \00312:28\004.","11/22/63","Stephen King",true},
},
["00:29"]={
{"“What time is it?” asked Teeny-bits.\nThe station agent hauled out his big silver watch, looked at it critically and announced: “\003Twenty-nine minutes past twelve\004.”\n“Past twelve!” repeated Teeny-bits. “It can’t be.”","The Mark of the Knife","Clayton H. Ernst",true},
},
["00:30"]={
{"\003Half-past twelve o’clock\004 came; Turkey began to glow in the face, overturn his inkstand, and become generally obstreperous; Nippers abated down into quietude and courtesy; Ginger Nut munched his noon apple; and Bartleby remained standing at his window in one of his profoundest dead-wall reveries.","Bartleby, the Scrivener","Herman Melville",true},
{"“I love you more than you can possibly know.”\n“I love you too.” I smile and his lips linger on my cheek. As he walks down the hall, I note the time: \003half past midnight\004.","Bath Haus","P.J. Vernon",true},
{"It was \003half-past twelve\004 when I returned to the Albany as a last desperate resort. The scene of my disaster was much as I had left it. The baccarat-counters still strewed the table, with the empty glasses and the loaded ash-trays. A window had been opened to let the smoke out, and was letting in the fog instead.","The Amateur Cracksman","E.W. Hornung",true},
},
["00:31"]={
{"Third individual approaches unnoticed and without caution. Once within reach, individual reaches out toward subjects. Recording terminates: timecode: \00300:31\004:02.","Zombie Apocalypse! Fightback","Stephen Jones",true},
},
["00:32"]={
{"Meticulously he noted the time by the wall clock over the fireplace and made a record in his book. “\00312:32\004 Mr. Courtney-Brigs reports fallen tree across the Winchester Road path.”","Shroud for a Nightingale","P.D. James",true},
{"\003Thirty-two minutes past midnight\004; the way things were going I could be at it all night. Before beginning a completely new search of the dial I had a thought: maybe this safe didn’t open on zero as older models did, but on a factory-set number.","Ixtapa","Everette Howard Hunt",true},
},
["00:33"]={
{"Stephen Maxie looked him straight in the eye and said almost casually: “It was \003thirty-three minutes past twelve\004 by my watch.”","Cover Her Face","P.D. James",true},
},
["00:34"]={
{"\003Thirty-four minutes past midnight\004. ‘We got ten minutes to be back here.’ LT didn’t argue. Schoolboy knew his former trade. LT’s eyes fretted over the museum. ‘Not still worrying about the security, are you, because there ain’t none.’","Killer Tune","Dreda Say Mitchell",true},
},
["00:35"]={
{"Mrs. Gentrie looked at the clock. It was \003thirty-five minutes past midnight\004.","The Case of the Empty Tin","Erle Stanley Gardner",true},
{"The clock read \003thirty-five minutes past midnight\004. I was dazed from the deepness of the sleep. Who could be calling me at this hour?","A Cat on the Cutting Edge","Lydia Adamson",true},
},
["00:36"]={
{"The prosecutor looked at her gold watch. \003Thirty-six minutes past midnight\004.","The Frozen Dead","Bernard Minier",true},
},
["00:37"]={
{"A glance at the luminous dial of his watch showed to be \003thirty-seven minutes past midnight\004.","Not a Marrying Man","Dixie Browning",true},
{"Stephen looked at his bedside clock. \00312:37 AM\004.\nHe went into the kitchen, and grabbed a Vanilla Coke from the refrigerator. In the living room, he opened the DVD cabinet, and ran his eyes across the hundreds of titles.","Warrior Monk","Ray Keating",true},
},
["00:38"]={
{"You left the main hospital building at about midnight. You spoke to the porter at the main gate at \003twelve thirty-eight a.m.\004 Where were you between those times?","Shroud for a Nightingale","P.D. James",true},
{"Somewhere he’d lost three days; for he’d entered the burning veil Thursday, \003thirty-eight minutes past midnight\004. Yes. But keep cool. There’s more at stake than three lost days. There must be; otherwise why the police?","Redemolished","Alfred Bester",true},
{"Justin turned on the light and groggily looked at the Sony clock radio which said it was \00312:38 a.m.\004 The screams in his dream had been painfully, frighteningly real, but he could not remember where the screams had come from.","Crow’s Nest","G.V. Miller",true},
},
["00:39"]={
{"It was \00312:39 a.m.\004 and I watched the moon fall prey to an evil-looking pack of galloping dark clouds.","Monastery Nightmare","Ross H. Spencer",true},
},
["00:40"]={
{"He looked around the carriage he was sitting in. It was full of night people, waiters, nurses, party returners, drunks—even a traffic warden. The train eventually pulled into his station at \003twelve-forty\004.","A Matter of Honor","Jeffrey Archer",true},
{"It was the opinion of the forensic pathologist who saw the body at \003twelve-forty\004 that Mrs. O’Keefe had died very shortly after her return home.","A Certain Justice","P.D. James",true},
{"\003Twenty minutes to one\004? exclaimed Helen. “My mother will certainly think we’re lost. But I hate to go. It is magnificent, even if it is terrible.”","White Ashes","Sidney R. Kennedy",true},
},
["00:41"]={
{"By the time he came back to his car, it was \00312:41 am\004. I was standing outside my car, just waiting and he noticed me.","Blood Ties","Geraldo Cruz",true},
},
["00:42"]={
{"The butt had been growing warm in her fingers; now the glowing end stung her skin. She crushed the cigarette out and stood, brushing ash from her black skirt. It was \003eighteen minutes to one\004. She went to the house phone and called his room. The telephone rang and rang, but there was no answer.","Marjorie Morningstar","Herman Wouk",true},
},
["00:43"]={
{"Died five minutes ago, you say? he asked. His eye went to the watch on his wrist. \003Twelve-forty-three\004, he wrote on the blotter.","A Pocket Full of Rye","Agatha Christie",true},
},
["00:44"]={
{"It was \00312:44 A.M.\004 when she turned the corner by Brulee’s onto Stateline Road. She waited on the approaching train.","Burning Embers","Wayne Pearson",true},
},
["00:45"]={
{"It was a banging shutter somewhere below that woke me. I picked my watch up from the night table and saw it was \003quarter of one\004. I didn’t think there was going to be any more sleep for me until that banging stopped, so I got dressed, started out the door, then returned to the closet for my slicker. When I got downstairs, I paused. From the big bedroom down the hall from the parlor, I could hear Mrs. S sawing wood in long, noisy strokes. No banging shutter was going to break her rest.","Joyland","Stephen King",true},
{"At \00312:45\004, during a lull, Mr. Yoshogi told me that owing to the war there were now many more women in England than men.","Pig and Pepper: A Comedy of Youth","David Footman",true},
{"At the thought he jumped to his feet and took down from its hook the coat in which he had left Miss Viner’s letter. The clock marked the \003third quarter after midnight\004, and he knew it would make no difference if he went down to the post-box now or early the next morning; but he wanted to clear his conscience, and having found the letter he went to the door.","The Reef","Edith Wharton",true},
},
["00:46"]={
{"Teddy wrote that phone records confirm Miss Lutton’s story. She called at \00312:46 a.m.\004","Dial M for Mischief","Kasey Michaels",true},
},
["00:47"]={
{"At \00312:47 a.m\004. Uncle Ho left us forever.","Last Night I Dreamed of Peace","Andrew X. Pham",true},
},
["00:48"]={
{"Stanton shut the light off, glancing quickly at the clock’s red numerals; it was \00312:48 a.m.\004 She tried to remember what day it was.","The Moriah Ruse","Marvin Wiebener",true},
},
["00:49"]={
{"That’s when they began yelling for help. A security guard at a nearby high-rise heard their cries and called police. It was \00312:49 A.M.\004 Metro-Dade Officer Bart Cohen and his partner arrived one minute later.","Never Let Them See You Cry","Edna Buchanan",true},
},
["00:50"]={
{"The packing was done at \00312:50\004; and Harris sat on the big hamper, and said he hoped nothing would be found broken. George said that if anything was broken it was broken, which reflection seemed to comfort him. He also said he was ready for bed.","Three Men in a Boat","Jerome K. Jerome",true},
},
["00:51"]={
{"My smile suddenly vanished after realizing the time. It was \00312:51\004 and at one in the morning usually checks us. I tried to run as fast as I could to reach the elevator until I did.","All the Stars Above Us","Jyerrmou",true},
},
["00:52"]={
{"New Year’s Eve night, well, way early New Year’s morning, 1998\nLet’s be exact: Let’s say it was \00312:52 a.m.\004\nI discovered what I want:\nAttention.","The Year of Lovemaking & Crying","Kenneth Robinson",true},
},
["00:53"]={
{"But he came out of it so slowly this time that Jacqueline had already picked up the phone and said hello before he was fully awake. The clock said it was \00312:53 A.M.\004 A bit early for Meade to call, yet who else could it be?","Impulse","Michael Weaver",true},
},
["00:54"]={
{"Everybody was happy; everybody was complimentary; the ice was soon broken; songs, anecdotes, and more drinks followed, and the pregnant minutes flew. At \003six minutes to one\004, when the jollity was at its highest— BOOM! There was silence instantly.","A Double Barrelled Detective Story","Mark Twain",true},
},
["00:55"]={
{"After a moment reality reasserted itself, and she realized she hadn’t been hallucinating, but dreaming. The clock on the desk read \00312:55\004. They’d begun their ten-minute session at 12:25, so obviously she had twenty minutes to account for.","The Enclave","Karen Hancock",true},
{"At \003five minutes to one\004, the host of the show emerged from a heated tent to massive applause from the crowd. She was dressed in a fuchsia coat, with a black turtleneck, a knee-length skirt, black tights, and knee-high boots.","The First Phone Call From Heaven","Mitch Albom",true},
{"He rolled one way, rolled the other, listened to the loud tick of the clock, and was asleep a minute later. \003Five to one\004 in the morning. Fifty-one hours to go.","61 Hours","Lee Child",true},
},
["00:56"]={
{"At \003twelve fifty-six A.M.\004, Jo O’Connor finally gave up on the idea of sleep. For hours she’d been awake worrying about Louis and Stormy and Sarah Two Knives. And about Cork.","Boundary Waters","William Kent Krueger",true},
{"It was \00312:56 A.M.\004 when Gerald drove up onto the grass and pulled the limousine right next to the cemetery.","Extremely Loud and Incredibly Close","Jonathan Safran Foer",true},
{"Teacher used to lie awake at night facing that clock, batting his eyelashes against his pillowcase to mimic the sound of the rolling drop action. One night, and this first night is lost in the countless later nights of compounding wonder, he discovered a game. Say the time was \00312:56\004.","Lessons in Essence","Dana Standridge",true},
},
["00:57"]={
{"A minute had passed, and the roller dropped a new leaf. \00312:57\004. 12 + 57 = 69; 6 + 9 = 15; 1 + 5 = 6. 712 + 5 = 717; 71 + 7 = 78; 7 + 8 = 15; 1 + 5 = 6 again.","Lessons in Essence","Dana Standridge",true},
},
["00:58"]={
{"It was downright shameless on his part to come visiting them, especially at night, \003almost at one in the morning\004, after all that had happened.","The Idiot","Fyodor Dostoyevsky",true},
{"\00300:58 CET\004\n“Everything’s in place. Now all we have to do is…”\nWilliam didn’t move a muscle until the voice faded away. More words, but they were scattered in the wind. He raised the tarpaulin an inch, and his eyes settled on a group of four men standing only a few yards from the lifeboat.","Nothing Ventured","Jeffrey Archer",true},
},
["00:59"]={
{"Only the hoot of a belated car faintly disturbed the silence.\nI looked at my wrist-watch. This showed \003one minute to one\004. As I raised my eyes, an impatient clock somewhere confirmed its tale.\nWith a yawn I conjured the terrier to go to sleep and reached for the switch.\nAs I did so, he growled again.","Berry and Co.","Dornford Yates",true},
{"What time is it now? she said.\n“\003About one o’clock\004.”\n“In the morning?”\nHerera’s friend leered at her. “No, there’s a total eclipse of the sun.”","Freedom","Jonathan Franzen",true},
{"It was \003nearly one o’clock\004 when Sherlock Holmes returned from his excursion. He held in his hand a sheet of blue paper, scrawled over with notes and figures.","The Adventures of Sherlock Holmes","Sir Arthur Conan Doyle",true},
{"I looked attentively at her, as she put that singular question to me. It was then \003nearly one o’clock\004. All I could discern distinctly by the moonlight was a colourless, youthful face, meagre and sharp to look at about the cheeks and chin; large, grave, wistfully attentive eyes; nervous, uncertain lips; and light hair of a pale, brownish-yellow hue.","The Woman in White","Wilkie Collins",true},
},
